{
  "description": "Shared cases for tooltip placeholders. text is a template text; fields are the fields its placeholders name, in order (a placeholder with a bad filter still names its field; an empty or nested one names none); problems are the kinds of mistake in order (unclosed, empty, nested, chained, later, unknown, arg; the sentences are each door's own); record is one item's row; shown is the text a reader sees for it: values go in as plain text and are never read again, a missing, null or blank value and an object or a list show the dash, text shows as typed whatever the filter, and a placeholder with a problem shows as written. Numbers follow the engine's number format (rounding ties to the even digit on the exact value, as R's sprintf; percent rounds the proportion to digits + 2 places and then moves the point). Every door that draws a template reads this file. A JSON file cannot hold Inf or NaN, so those cases are not here: they show the dash.",
